From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:03:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: decoder: Make the probed caps writable before
 filtering

When none of the driver's capture formats maps to a known format, the
intersection with the template caps is empty, and
gst_caps_intersect_full() returns a reference to the shared
GST_CAPS_NONE. gst_v4l2_decoder_enum_src_formats_full() then filters
and appends to it in place, which fails the writability assertions of
gst_caps_filter_and_map_in_place() and gst_caps_append(). Seen with the
Raspberry Pi HEVC decoder on 10-bit streams, whose column formats
v4l2codecs did not know.
---
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2decoder.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2decoder.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2decoder.c
@@ -599,6 +599,8 @@ gst_v4l2_decoder_enum_src_formats_full (
   gst_caps_unref (tmp);
   gst_caps_unref (filter);
 
+  /* An empty intersection is the shared GST_CAPS_NONE */
+  caps = gst_caps_make_writable (caps);
   tmp = gst_caps_copy (caps);
   gst_caps_filter_and_map_in_place (caps, filter_only_dmabuf_caps, NULL);
   gst_caps_filter_and_map_in_place (tmp, filter_non_dmabuf_caps, NULL);
